Package: ForestFireR
Type: Package
Title: Spatial and Mean-Field Forest-Fire Invasion Model
Version: 0.4.01
Author: Leonardo A. Saravia, Rebeca de la Fuente
Maintainer: Leonardo A. Saravia <lasaravia@untdf.edu.ar>
Description: R/Rcpp interface to a spatial stochastic (Gillespie) and
    deterministic mean-field model of fire-driven biological invasion in a
    two-species, fire-vegetation system. Provides R-friendly functions,
    using a compact dimensionless notation (xi, eta, p) for fire spread,
    post-fire regrowth and spatial heterogeneity, to generate initial
    landscapes and run spatially-explicit or well-mixed simulations with
    full trajectory/snapshot recording. Based on the original
    forest_fire_model.cpp engine, with missing grid-index-mapping
    functions restored, dynamic grid sizing, reproducible RNG seeding, and
    a numerically stable mean-field integrator added. The model is
    described in de la Fuente & Saravia, "Dynamics of invasion in
    forest-fire models" -- see the README for citation details.
